From ec793506f9d6c78a487a96a1421e4620eeaa74b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:55:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] PartDesign: New Body and dropping onto a body share one base
 feature test

PR #31763 ("PD: Allow BaseFeatures from other App::Parts") let a body take a
base feature from another App::Part (STEP imports with nested Part
containers) and from links. For the links it widened the selection
PartDesign_Body looks at from Part::Feature to every App::DocumentObject, and
the drop test of ViewProviderBody from Part::Feature to "has a non-null
shape". Since then every selected object is a base feature candidate: a
Spreadsheet or VarSet still selected after its creation, a mesh, points, a
coordinate system or an origin gives the modal "Base feature (...) has an
empty shape."; an App::Part, a group or a link group becomes the BaseFeature
(a compound of its children; the active App::Part even a body based on its
own container); an origin plane or axis gives an infinite base; a mixed
selection fails with "Body may be based on no more than one feature." and no
body. Dropping a group, an App::Part or a link group onto an empty body makes
it the BaseFeature as well.

PartDesignGui::canBeBaseFeature() (Utils) now answers the question for both
paths: the object owns Part geometry (Part::Feature, or a GeoFeature whose
geometry property is a Part shape), directly or as the final target of a
link, a link array or a chain of them. Links are followed with
LinkBaseExtension::getTrueLinkedObject(), because getLinkedObject() stops at
a link array (extensionGetLinkedObject() returns the array itself while
ElementCount > 0); a link group has no target and stays out.

PartDesign_Body leaves the other selected objects out silently, as before
#31763. Shape objects keep every check and message: other body, Part Design
feature, body, sketch, the empty-shape warning of a Part feature without a
shape, the multiple solids/shells warnings, links and link arrays of solids,
base features from other App::Parts. The BaseFeature/move branch of
canDropObject() requires canBeBaseFeature() in addition to a non-empty shape;
its VarSet, datum, coordinate system, sub-shape binder and 2D object branches
are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
